  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​810 — November 10, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192692/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0 12px;\"><p>JavaScript Weekly</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192646/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/oxtotle26xtvjolphndc.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192646/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.x.com\">How X (Twitter) is Rebuilding Its Web App</a></span> — X is replacing 3 servers with one app built on React, Vite and Fastify. Yagiz, famed for his performance work on Node, explains the streaming architecture behind it, along with some bottlenecks they had to fix, like how hundreds of tiny JavaScript files slowed startup.</p>\n<p>Yagiz Nizipli (X Engineering Blog) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192645/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"145\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/966f3f3a.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"145\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192645/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"link.svix.com\">Why Standard Webhooks Hit 118m npm Downloads a Month</a></span> — OpenAI, Anthropic, and Gemini all sign webhooks with Standard Webhooks, the open spec Svix started. That's one finding in the State of Webhooks 2027, where we scored 489 API companies on retries and signatures. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192645/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Immediate download, no email required</a>.</p>\n<p>Svix <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192647/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"v3.parceljs.org\">Parcel 3 Alpha: The Bundler Rewritten in Rust</a></span> — A ground-up Rust rewrite of the popular bundler that the team reports is up to 100x faster than Parcel 2 at cold builds of React Spectrum. It runs as a standalone binary without Node, with support for native plugins written in Rust, Go or Swift, while JavaScript plugins run on an embedded QuickJS runtime.</p>\n<p>The Parcel Team </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>📊 The <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192648/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">State of JavaScript 2026 survey is now open</a>. Share the features, libraries and tools you use and like, and discover a few new ones along the way. We'll share the results once they're out.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>TypeScript 7's Go-powered compiler now has <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192649/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">an experimental WebAssembly build</a> which already powers an early <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192650/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">TypeScript Playground v2</a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>ESLint <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192651/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">now officially lints shell scripts</a> with the <code>@eslint/shell</code> plugin adding ShellCheck-like rules for Bash, sh and mksh.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>RELEASES:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192652/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Playwright 1.65</a> – The browser testing tool's test runner can now run under Bun, plus there's a new failures reporter.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192653/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Storybook 11 Beta</a> – The UI component workshop gets more agent-ready, with official skills, Claude/Codex plugins, headless CLI tools, and more.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 Vite has disclosed <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192654/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">a critical remote code execution flaw</a> affecting <em>dev</em> servers exposed to the network via <code>--host</code> or <code>server.host</code>. Upgrade to 8.3.7, 8.2.5, 8.1.7, 7.3.8 or 6.4.6.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 Next.js <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192655/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">16.4.5 and 15.5.29 fix seven security issues</a>, including a high-severity cross-tenant cache disclosure.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🔒 Node.js <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192656/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">security releases are due tomorrow</a> (or shortly after) for the 26.x, 24.x and 22.x lines.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📖  Articles and Videos</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192657/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/yjfttwj00vb3oqvzibqd.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192657/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"blog.arv.tools\">Experiments with Multithreaded JavaScript</a></span> — What would JavaScript look like if threads could share objects directly? Former TC39 delegate Erik Arvidsson explores three approaches: in a <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192658/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Porffor</a> fork, as a TypeScript library with an ownership checker, and as an implementation of the <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192659/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">TC39 structs proposal</a>. Each has a playground to try.</p>\n<p>Erik Arvidsson </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192660/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nodejs.org\">The New JavaScript Features Between V8 14.6 and 15.6</a></span> — Node 27, released in alpha recently, is built on V8 15.6, and Joyee tours what that brings to developers, including <code>Math.sumPrecise</code>, new iterator methods, and some behavior changes in sorting, dates and promises, all with sample code.</p>\n<p>Joyee Cheung </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192661/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"sentry.io\">How to Build Your Own Automated Debugging Workflow</a></span> — Connect your coding agent to Sentry and turn errors into fix PRs. See the guides and recipes in the resource hub.</p>\n<p>Sentry <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192662/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"mofu-dev.com\">Spreading Liquid with <code>three.js</code></a></span> — A technical explanation of a 'liquid-spreading' effect originally built for a cosmetics site. The in-page demo is fun to play with and this could be handy if you want to create paint-like effects.</p>\n<p>Misaki Nakano </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192663/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"jamesbox.exe.xyz\">Reviving Facebook's Abandoned JavaScript Optimizer</a></span> — Prettier creator James Long put agents to work resurrecting <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192664/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Prepack</a>, Facebook's attempt to make JavaScript faster by running it ahead of time. There's <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192665/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">an experimental demo</a> that shows off the gains on a sample React app.</p>\n<p>James Long </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192666/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"yavashark.dev\">Yavashark: Building a JavaScript Engine for 950 Days Straight</a></span> — A solo developer's progress report on a Rust-based engine they're building that passes around 82% of test262 and can server-render a React app. There's <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192667/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">a playground</a> to try it for yourself.</p>\n<p>Sharktheone </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192668/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">A Fifth Object Shape Made the Same Loop Twice as Slow</a> – V8's hidden classes and inline caches in action. <cite>Mohsen Fallahnejad</cite></p>\n<p>📺 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192669/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">ReactiveScript: Early Findings</a> – A lengthy stream by Solid's creator on <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192670/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">ReactiveScript</a>, his experimental reactive UI language he <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192671/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">first shared in 2021</a>. <cite>Ryan Carniato</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠 Code &amp; Tools</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192672/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/mhgipfuzi5v4n6zlnbaj.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192672/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.embedpdf.com\">EmbedPDF 3.0: A PDF Viewer for Any JavaScript App</a></span> — An open-source PDF viewer for vanilla JavaScript, React, Vue, Svelte and Angular. The <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192673/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">v3 rebuild</a> offers a ready-made viewer, headless components for custom UIs, and a standalone PDF engine. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192674/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Try the demo.</a></p>\n<p>EmbedPDF </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192675/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"playground.developers.thinkfree.com\">Embed an Office Editor Your App's AI Agent Can Use</a></span> — DOCX/XLSX/PPTX editing in your app with your model and workflow. Agents make targeted edits, and users refine the file.</p>\n<p>Thinkfree <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #993 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192676/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">chrome-capture: Record a Chrome Tab at 60-120fps to an MP4 File</a></span> — It's been <em>three</em> years since we've linked to Paul Irish (once a frequent fixture in JavaScript Weekly!) but he's back with a neat, compact tool you can run with <code>npx</code> to record a Chrome tab at high quality <em>including audio</em> to an <code>MP4</code> video.</p>\n<p>Paul Irish </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192677/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"textjs.org\">Text.js: React Apps That Render in the Browser Console</a></span> — Really! A React 19 framework whose 'screen' is the DevTools console, with routing, keyboard input, layout primitives and ASCII fonts. Open the console on the homepage to try it, then <code>bunx create-text-app</code> if you're tempted. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192678/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub repo.</a></p>\n<p>Anomaly </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192679/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.jeasx.dev\">Jeasx 3.0: Server-Rendered JSX, Now Streaming</a></span> — A minimal framework that uses JSX purely as a server-side templating language (with no React and no hydration) on top of Fastify and esbuild. v3 streams pages while async components are still loading and renders ~2x faster. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192680/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\">Live examples.</a></p>\n<p>Jeasx </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192681/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Rolldown 1.3</a> – The Rust-powered bundler adds experimental support for import attributes, but there are breaking changes to be aware of.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192682/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">jsdom 31.0</a> – The pure JS implementation of DOM/HTML standards adds a new CSS engine and switches to a Skia-backed canvas backend.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192683/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Remix 3.2</a> – The full-stack framework adds nonce-based Content Security Policy middleware.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192684/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Wiki.js 3.3</a> – Open source JavaScript and Node.js-powered wiki app.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📺 <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192685/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">JetBrains AI.js Day 2026</a>: Frontend's scariest AI questions answered live on channel 13, Nov 13. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192685/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Register now!</a></p>\n<p>🔑 One subscription, a dozen people. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192686/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Fingerprint</a> shows how many devices are really behind each account. <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192686/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Try it free</a>.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192687/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/lpocbjy3uza3w1yogw1i.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>📺 I've been enjoying Arjay McCandless's YouTube channel lately as he's been focusing on maxing out VPSes with different stacks (and often being surprised by the results). This time, he <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192687/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">compares 22 combinations of JavaScript runtimes and frameworks</a> to see how many users they can handle!</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🌙 Safari 27.3 beta introduces <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192688/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">Adaptive Dark Mode</a>, an opt-in feature that automatically darkens light websites that don't provide their own dark theme.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🎨 Three.js creator mrdoob is posting <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192689/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">daily visual experiments for Codevember</a>, complete with live demos and source.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>💰 Cloudflare has <a href=\"https://javascriptweekly.com/link/192690/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3366aa; font-weight: 500;\" target=\"_blank\">handed out the first $301,300</a> of the $1M <em>Vite Ecosystem Fund</em> it pledged when VoidZero joined, spread across 44 projects and maintainers, including e18e.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
